      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "An unprecedented α-hydroxylation strategy was developed for the synthesis of α-hydroxy arones using N,N-dimethylformamide (DMF) as an oxygen source. Control experiments demonstrated that the oxygen atom of the hydroxy group in the α-hydroxy arones produced in this reaction was derived from DMF. This new reaction therefore not only provides an alternative strategy for the α-hydroxylation of arones but also highlights the possibility of using the inexpensive common solvent DMF as a source of oxygen in organic synthesis."},
